rs with Mining. Guns and scopes only improve Shoot, which a Rogue uses for pulling."},{n="Alchemy",b="Agility and Strength elixirs, healing potions and protection potions for hard fights.",cv="Ordinary healing potions are also First Aid crafts in Forever; discolored Alchemy potions have a different effect."},{n="Herbalism",b="Herbs for Alchemy or income. Sap and Vanish let a Rogue gather herbs past enemies, even inside dungeons.",cv="Swiftthistle for Thistle Tea is a bonus herb from Mageroyal and Briarthorn."},{n="Mining",b="Ore and stone for Blacksmithing or Engineering, and income from bars.",cv="No direct combat bonus beyond the gathering itself."},{n=S[60],b="Rough Sharpening Stones and Rough Weightstones early, which have a big impact at low level, plus daggers, swords, axes and maces to compare.",cv="You can buy the stones instead. Most plate and mail recipes are of no use to a Rogue."},{n="Cooking",b="Buff food that adds stats and extra experience from kills; Thistle Tea (Cooking 60, from the poison quest) restores 100 Energy.",cv="Thistle Tea has a 5-minute cooldown."},{n="First Aid",b="Bandages, healing potions and Anti-Venom. Rogues have no healing spells, so this is the main way to recover in a fight: Blind or Gouge, then bandage.",cv="Damage interrupts bandaging."},{n="Fishing",b="Fish for Cooking, including buff-food ingredients.",cv="No guaranteed income is implied."}},gearBrackets={{b="Quest rewards",no="Quest rewards that fit this spec's stat priority, sorted by quest level. The tooltip names the quest, its level, the quest giver and the faction. Quest level is not the minimum pickup level.",keys={"st-rogue-3","st-rogue-2","st-rogue-1","rogue-g65","rogue-g17","rogue-g88","rogue-g89","rogue-g47","rogue-g16","rogue-g14","rogue-g34","rogue-g71","rogue-g76","rogue-g90","rogue-g127","rogue-g106","rogue-g119","rogue-g77","rogue-g23","rogue-g0","rogue-g3","rogue-g15","rogue-g92","rogue-g6","rogue-g8","rogue-g24","rogue-g26","rogue-g85","rogue-g111","rogue-g